1
00:00:00,967 --> 00:00:02,867
<i>Can't you just do it
online instead?</i>

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,233
<i> Mom, I'll be right back.</i>

3
00:00:04,367 --> 00:00:05,333
<i> You better be.</i>

4
00:00:05,467 --> 00:00:06,300
<i> Take care too, Mom.</i>

5
00:00:06,433 --> 00:00:07,400
<i> Joey, let's go?</i>

6
00:00:07,533 --> 00:00:08,700
<i>I don't even know where to start</i>

7
00:00:08,833 --> 00:00:10,467
<i> once we get to Valmora.</i>

8
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:12,433
<i>I've got it covered,
I know someone there.</i>

9
00:00:12,567 --> 00:00:14,200
<i>- Who?
- Zoey.</i>

10
00:00:14,333 --> 00:00:16,100
<i> Andrew, what brings you here?</i>

11
00:00:16,233 --> 00:00:17,233
<i> I'm swallowing my pride...</i>

12
00:00:17,367 --> 00:00:18,300
<i> I need your help.</i>

13
00:00:18,433 --> 00:00:20,433
<i>Dad? Dad, wait!
Dad!</i>

14
00:00:20,567 --> 00:00:21,467
<i> What's all that noise?</i>

15
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:22,567
<i> We thought you were cops!</i>

16
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:24,133
<i>Looks like this pretty one
is lost.</i>

17
00:00:24,267 --> 00:00:25,367
<i> Want us to help you?</i>

18
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,900
<i>Miss, did you see the girl I was
with earlier?</i>

19
00:00:28,033 --> 00:00:30,567
<i>She left,
she went that way.</i>

20
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:31,900
<i> Come on, let's talk inside.</i>

21
00:00:32,033 --> 00:00:33,000
<i> Let go of me!</i>

22
00:00:35,033 --> 00:00:36,167
<i> Come here, Andrew!</i>

23
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:37,967
<i>I've got too many enemies,
I can't handle them alone!</i>

24
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:40,633
<i>Where do you think you're going?
Your luck's running out.</i>

25
00:00:44,167 --> 00:00:45,933
<i> Cops! Let's go!</i>

26
00:00:46,067 --> 00:00:47,967
<i> Joey, this is Zoey.</i>

27
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:51,100
<i>She'll be helping us
while we're here in Valmora.</i>

28
00:00:51,233 --> 00:00:52,867
<i>I'm his ex-girlfriend
by the way.</i>

29
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,967
<i> I thought Joey was a guy.</i>

30
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:58,100
<i>Is there a problem
if his friend's a girl?</i>

31
00:00:58,233 --> 00:01:00,200
<i> Depends, how close are you?</i>

32
00:01:00,333 --> 00:01:01,367
<i>- What's that?
- Take a look.</i>

33
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,400
<i>Don't tell me you're giving me
a makeover?</i>

34
00:01:03,533 --> 00:01:05,467
<i> Yes, just follow my advice.</i>

35
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,633
<i> Why did you leave the eatery?</i>

36
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:09,567
<i> I thought I saw my dad.</i>

37
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:11,233
<i>I really feel like
he's still alive...</i>

38
00:01:11,367 --> 00:01:13,100
<i>and he's here looking
for Berdugo.</i>

39
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:14,633
<i> Berdugo?</i>

40
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,767
Now, it's your time.

41
00:02:09,167 --> 00:02:10,667
Yes! Yes!

42
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:12,933
Faster! Faster!

43
00:02:16,633 --> 00:02:18,367
Sorry, sorry!

44
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:19,567
No!

45
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:21,033
Use your shoulder!

46
00:02:21,167 --> 00:02:22,500
I'll show you.

47
00:02:23,233 --> 00:02:26,100
One, two, three, four!

48
00:02:28,467 --> 00:02:29,433
Eight...

49
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:30,367
nine...

50
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:31,833
last one!

51
00:02:35,167 --> 00:02:36,400
Whoo!

52
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:43,100
I've prepared people to go
with you on your trip.

53
00:02:43,233 --> 00:02:44,800
And the cargo?

54
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:12,367
Berdugo, how are you, my dear?

55
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:15,300
Delilah, I'm all set
for my trip.

56
00:03:16,967 --> 00:03:18,733
And the samples?

57
00:03:18,867 --> 00:03:19,767
Ready.

58
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:21,533
<i> These products are topnotch.</i>

59
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:23,367
You won't be disappointed.

60
00:03:24,333 --> 00:03:27,833
Well, to taste and experience
is to believe.

61
00:03:27,967 --> 00:03:29,467
I'm looking forward
to put a face

62
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,800
to the mysterious Berdugo.

63
00:03:31,933 --> 00:03:33,700
I'll see you soon, my dear.

64
00:03:40,667 --> 00:03:42,400
So your theory is Berdugo
will replace

65
00:03:42,533 --> 00:03:45,267
Godfather as the supplier
here in Valmora?

66
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:47,800
Seems like it,
that's why I came to you

67
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:50,400
I know you can use this lead.

68
00:03:50,533 --> 00:03:52,233
You know, Andrew,

69
00:03:52,367 --> 00:03:54,967
you could've told me
all of that over the phone.

70
00:03:55,767 --> 00:03:58,367
Why come here in Valmora?

71
00:03:59,433 --> 00:04:01,367
For Joey?

72
00:04:03,433 --> 00:04:05,533
You're such a kind friend,

73
00:04:05,667 --> 00:04:08,033
and dedicated journalist.

74
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:13,833
Of course I want to be the first
to expose Berdugo.

75
00:04:13,967 --> 00:04:15,467
Oh, right.

76
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:17,267
Exposé.

77
00:04:23,033 --> 00:04:24,700
Why isn't it here.

78
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:27,400
- Joey?
- It's not here.

79
00:04:28,033 --> 00:04:29,400
Wait, what happened?

80
00:04:29,533 --> 00:04:32,500
The keychain my dad gave me,
it's gone.

81
00:04:33,767 --> 00:04:37,233
Maybe you dropped it
when you fought those addicts.

82
00:04:37,633 --> 00:04:38,967
Ah, okay, Joey...

83
00:04:39,100 --> 00:04:42,767
Tomorrow, we'll go back for it
if needed.

84
00:05:13,767 --> 00:05:15,433
Nice one.

85
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,333
No wonder...

86
00:05:18,467 --> 00:05:20,967
you have a great body...

87
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:23,100
you're really good at abs.

88
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:25,867
You deserve a reward...

89
00:05:27,133 --> 00:05:28,500
Coffee...

90
00:05:28,633 --> 00:05:30,067
with me?

91
00:05:30,933 --> 00:05:33,033
Ah, pass.

92
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:35,633
Who is that?

93
00:05:37,833 --> 00:05:39,367
That's confusing.

94
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:42,067
I didn't say anything wrong.

95
00:05:48,167 --> 00:05:49,100
You know what?

96
00:05:49,233 --> 00:05:51,800
Your tone, your attitude...

97
00:05:51,933 --> 00:05:54,233
You look like a creep!

98
00:05:54,367 --> 00:05:55,933
What? A perv?

99
00:05:56,433 --> 00:05:57,500
No!

100
00:05:57,633 --> 00:05:59,467
She's just picky.

101
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:01,600
I didn't say anything bad.

102
00:06:03,933 --> 00:06:05,900
What should it be then?
Go on, you.

103
00:06:06,033 --> 00:06:07,367
How?

104
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:12,700
Watch and learn, okay?

105
00:06:15,733 --> 00:06:17,300
<i> Hello.</i>

106
00:06:27,667 --> 00:06:30,767
But still,
kudos for your effort.

107
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:33,100
I'm sorry,
but I didn't understand.

108
00:06:33,233 --> 00:06:35,467
But still, thank you.

109
00:06:58,167 --> 00:06:59,200
See?

110
00:06:59,333 --> 00:07:00,833
It's easy.

111
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:02,833
You're amazing, Oppa but...

112
00:07:02,967 --> 00:07:04,467
what did you say?

113
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:07,567
I told her her form
is dangerous,

114
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:09,067
she could injure herself,

115
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:11,933
and the shoes are not ideal.

116
00:07:12,533 --> 00:07:13,833
That's it?

117
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,933
You shut her down
but she still liked it?

118
00:07:16,067 --> 00:07:17,500
I told you.

119
00:07:17,633 --> 00:07:19,233
It's not what you say.

120
00:07:19,367 --> 00:07:20,733
It's how you say it.

121
00:07:20,867 --> 00:07:21,800
No, no.

122
00:07:21,933 --> 00:07:23,600
I think it's the language.

123
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:25,733
you just acted like an oppa
and she already got excited.

124
00:07:25,867 --> 00:07:28,067
Unfair! That's so unfair.

125
00:07:29,333 --> 00:07:31,633
So next time, when you see Joey,

126
00:07:31,767 --> 00:07:33,067
you know what to do.

127
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:38,200
Just remember, posture, form,
eye contact.

128
00:07:39,367 --> 00:07:41,533
Sure you noticed the difference.

129
00:07:43,333 --> 00:07:44,733
I don't know, Oppa.

130
00:07:44,867 --> 00:07:47,700
Do I really need all of this
just for her to notice me?

131
00:07:49,067 --> 00:07:51,167
You're a good guy, Peter.

132
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:53,767
You will be good for Joey.

133
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:56,567
She just need to see you
in a different light.

134
00:07:56,700 --> 00:07:58,633
I'll get it, Oppa.

135
00:07:59,733 --> 00:08:02,500
You will figure out
the timing eventually.

136
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:06,100
And please stop calling me
"oppa."

137
00:08:06,233 --> 00:08:08,800
Oppa is only used by girls.

138
00:08:09,733 --> 00:08:11,667
So what should I call you
instead?

139
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:13,200
Call me "hyung," okay?

140
00:08:13,333 --> 00:08:14,533
- Hyung?
- Yes, hyung.

141
00:08:14,667 --> 00:08:17,633
Only because we are good,
true friends now.

142
00:08:17,767 --> 00:08:19,500
No, I', not use to this,
I'm used calling you oppa.

143
00:08:19,633 --> 00:08:21,067
- Just Oppa then.
- No, no.

144
00:08:21,233 --> 00:08:22,733
- Hyung.
- No, no. Oppa.

145
00:08:22,867 --> 00:08:25,067
- Hyung! Hyung!
- Oppa!

146
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:26,467
Oppa.

147
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:29,700
If you don't,
you will regret it.

148
00:08:29,833 --> 00:08:31,667
Oh, I'm so scared.

149
00:08:31,800 --> 00:08:34,233
Oppa...
Oppa...

150
00:08:34,367 --> 00:08:36,533
Oppa...

151
00:08:37,467 --> 00:08:39,133
Oppa, huh?

152
00:08:39,267 --> 00:08:41,267
You can stay here
as long as you need.

153
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:42,667
I live alone anyway...

154
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:46,000
and frankly,
I welcome the company.

155
00:08:46,467 --> 00:08:47,867
Thank you, Zoey.

156
00:08:48,533 --> 00:08:50,533
Once I find my dad,

157
00:08:50,667 --> 00:08:52,367
I won't be a burden anymore.

158
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:53,933
No problem.

159
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:57,333
Andrew, can I talk to you?

160
00:08:57,467 --> 00:08:58,667
Just for a bit.

161
00:09:04,767 --> 00:09:06,200
Sure.

162
00:09:34,367 --> 00:09:35,600
Hello?

163
00:09:35,733 --> 00:09:37,000
Joey...

164
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:50,467
Dad?

165
00:09:54,367 --> 00:09:55,700
Joey, my child...

166
00:10:00,267 --> 00:10:01,900
I knew it.

167
00:10:02,067 --> 00:10:03,967
I never believed
you were dead, Dad.

168
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:06,067
I felt that you were
still alive.

169
00:10:07,867 --> 00:10:09,467
Who's with you there?

170
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,367
No one.

171
00:10:15,367 --> 00:10:19,000
Don't tell Andrew
that you're talking to me.

172
00:10:19,133 --> 00:10:21,433
How did you know
Andrew's with me?

173
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,400
Dad?

174
00:10:35,933 --> 00:10:37,200
Dad!

175
00:10:37,967 --> 00:10:39,700
I was right!

176
00:10:39,833 --> 00:10:42,167
You're the man
I was following earlier.

177
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,567
<i> But, Dad, how did that happen?</i>

178
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:46,500
Wasn't your car completely
burned?

179
00:10:46,633 --> 00:10:48,000
How did you get here?

180
00:10:48,133 --> 00:10:49,867
Why didn't you come home to us?

181
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:52,267
<i> It's a long story, Joey.</i>

182
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:54,700
When I returned to service,

183
00:10:54,833 --> 00:10:56,633
<i> I felt that...</i>

184
00:10:57,333 --> 00:10:59,567
my life was in danger.

185
00:11:00,733 --> 00:11:02,633
<i> Oh, sorry...</i>

186
00:11:05,567 --> 00:11:08,600
I saw a man outside the station.

187
00:11:08,767 --> 00:11:10,567
<i>He's the same guy
who caused trouble</i>

188
00:11:10,700 --> 00:11:12,500
while Andrew was
interviewing me.

189
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:23,067
<i> Hey!</i>

190
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:26,000
And he's also the man
I saw at our house!

191
00:11:26,133 --> 00:11:27,767
<i> At our house?</i>

192
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:29,933
<i> Okay, Dad, please be careful.</i>

193
00:11:41,067 --> 00:11:42,133
<i> Hey!</i>

194
00:12:04,533 --> 00:12:06,067
<i> Go ahead, chase me.</i>

195
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:07,600
<i> Leave my family alone!</i>

196
00:12:07,733 --> 00:12:10,167
<i>Is he the man who tried
to kill you?</i>

197
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:11,233
Yes, Joey.

198
00:12:11,367 --> 00:12:12,867
We fought.

199
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:20,467
After that, I saw he was
carrying a photo...

200
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:22,733
<i> A photo of our family.</i>

201
00:12:24,667 --> 00:12:26,700
<i>Don't drag my family into this!</i>

202
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:30,900
You want to save your family?

203
00:12:31,967 --> 00:12:33,333
<i> Then you'll die!</i>

204
00:12:33,467 --> 00:12:35,100
But I couldn't do anything...

205
00:13:13,367 --> 00:13:16,300
<i> Chief, I need help.</i>

206
00:13:18,933 --> 00:13:20,733
<i> I knew it, Dad.</i>

207
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:22,133
I had a feeling...

208
00:13:22,267 --> 00:13:24,067
Chief Lansang was hiding
something from me.

209
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:26,500
<i>That's why he didn't want
to show us your body.</i>

210
00:13:26,967 --> 00:13:27,733
<i> And you know what?</i>

211
00:13:27,867 --> 00:13:29,067
Even Mom, she refuses
to believe it.

212
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:31,200
She doesn't want to hope
that you're still alive.

213
00:13:32,367 --> 00:13:35,733
Joey, I understand why
your mother feels that way.

214
00:13:36,967 --> 00:13:40,100
Because, Dad, what you did
to us really hurt.

215
00:13:40,233 --> 00:13:42,300
You made us look like fools.

216
00:13:42,433 --> 00:13:47,500
We mourned someone,
who was actually still alive.

217
00:13:51,233 --> 00:13:53,767
You know, you still
haven't changed.

218
00:13:55,967 --> 00:13:57,433
You're still handsome.

219
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:02,733
Maybe you've matured,
just a little.

220
00:14:04,233 --> 00:14:05,700
Oh.

221
00:14:05,833 --> 00:14:07,700
Well, I am getting older.

222
00:14:09,067 --> 00:14:11,567
It's been...

223
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:13,033
four years...

224
00:14:13,167 --> 00:14:15,133
since we last saw each other.

225
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:18,600
I don't think it's age.

226
00:14:19,933 --> 00:14:21,800
Stress.

227
00:14:21,933 --> 00:14:23,800
Well, it's a stressful job.

228
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:30,000
I really want to get
this exposé.

229
00:14:30,633 --> 00:14:32,433
Is that really what you want?

230
00:14:33,767 --> 00:14:35,500
Are you sure about that?

231
00:14:38,233 --> 00:14:39,833
What else?

232
00:14:41,933 --> 00:14:43,433
Well...

233
00:14:44,067 --> 00:14:45,167
Joey's pretty.

234
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:47,733
It's not hard to be attracted
to her.

235
00:14:48,333 --> 00:14:53,733
- Maybe you're doing this...
- to help my friend.

236
00:14:55,167 --> 00:14:56,567
That's all there is to it.

237
00:14:57,333 --> 00:15:00,367
So you can honestly say
you don't like her?

238
00:15:01,267 --> 00:15:02,667
Look, ah...

239
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:04,167
Zoey...

240
00:15:06,033 --> 00:15:09,767
This mission
is my priority right now.

241
00:15:11,267 --> 00:15:14,000
I don't have any other
intention but that...

242
00:15:14,133 --> 00:15:17,400
and to help my friend Joey.

243
00:15:17,533 --> 00:15:19,800
Please don't read
anything else into it.

244
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:24,000
All right, fine.

245
00:15:24,133 --> 00:15:25,733
I'm just asking.

246
00:15:36,967 --> 00:15:37,900
- Bro.
- Oh.

247
00:15:38,033 --> 00:15:39,300
I'll go ahead.

248
00:15:39,433 --> 00:15:40,567
You're leaving already?

249
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:41,933
Let's hang out for a bit,
my treat.

250
00:15:42,067 --> 00:15:43,867
Let's have a drink.

251
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:45,933
It's my way of thanking you
for all the lessons

252
00:15:46,067 --> 00:15:47,533
and the makeover.

253
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:49,500
I can't.

254
00:15:49,633 --> 00:15:50,600
Why?

255
00:15:50,733 --> 00:15:52,467
Someone waiting for you?

256
00:15:54,433 --> 00:15:56,100
Hey, don't think I forgot.

257
00:15:56,233 --> 00:15:57,933
You still owe me.

258
00:15:58,067 --> 00:15:59,933
You haven't told me
where you've been

259
00:16:00,067 --> 00:16:01,033
or what you've been doing.

260
00:16:01,167 --> 00:16:02,467
I even asked your landlady.

261
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:03,867
She got mad at me.

262
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,467
You looked for me?

263
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:06,667
Of course!

264
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:07,700
I was worried about you.

265
00:16:07,833 --> 00:16:10,567
For all I knew,
you were already dead...

266
00:16:10,733 --> 00:16:12,300
because of some syndicate.

267
00:16:14,833 --> 00:16:19,500
I mean, I didn't realize
that you care for me like that.

268
00:16:19,633 --> 00:16:22,333
Of course, we're friends, right?

269
00:16:22,467 --> 00:16:25,100
Joey said we're solid, right?

270
00:16:25,233 --> 00:16:28,300
You know, if Joey's dad
weren't dead,

271
00:16:29,167 --> 00:16:31,067
I'm sure he'd be looking
for you too.

272
00:16:34,067 --> 00:16:36,600
I'm sorry I didn't tell you
that I moved.

273
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,600
You moved?

274
00:16:38,733 --> 00:16:39,567
Where?

275
00:16:39,700 --> 00:16:41,667
Somewhere closer
where Theresa might be.

276
00:16:41,833 --> 00:16:43,133
What?

277
00:16:43,267 --> 00:16:44,133
That's dangerous.

278
00:16:44,267 --> 00:16:46,000
Do you have a death wish
or something?

279
00:16:46,133 --> 00:16:47,133
Don't worry.

280
00:16:47,267 --> 00:16:48,900
I'm being very careful.

281
00:16:49,033 --> 00:16:50,633
I trust you...

282
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:54,900
Mr. Intelligence Agent.

283
00:16:56,900 --> 00:16:57,933
Just don't disappear again

284
00:16:58,067 --> 00:17:00,067
without telling me,
okay, Oppa?

285
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,233
- It's hyung.
- Oppa.

286
00:17:02,367 --> 00:17:03,367
Hyung.

287
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:05,100
- Oppa.
- Hyung.

288
00:17:05,233 --> 00:17:08,167
Okay, fine.

289
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:14,467
<i> I'm sorry, Joey,</i>

290
00:17:14,600 --> 00:17:15,800
<i> but this is the only way</i>

291
00:17:15,967 --> 00:17:18,333
<i> to make sure you're safe.</i>

292
00:17:19,333 --> 00:17:21,600
I'm the syndicate's target...

293
00:17:22,233 --> 00:17:23,933
and I know they won't stop

294
00:17:24,067 --> 00:17:26,200
<i> until I'm dead.</i>

295
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:30,500
It hurts me to lie to you...

296
00:17:31,333 --> 00:17:33,467
but I'm doing all this for you.

297
00:17:33,933 --> 00:17:35,900
But, Dad, what do we do now?

298
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,400
Are you really going
to pretend you're dead?

299
00:17:40,067 --> 00:17:42,800
<i>Dad, does this mean we can't be
with you and Mom anymore?</i>

300
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:45,233
No, Joey.

301
00:17:46,767 --> 00:17:48,767
I know Berdugo's plan.

302
00:17:50,533 --> 00:17:52,600
I will bring down the syndicate.

303
00:17:52,733 --> 00:17:55,733
<i>After that,
we'll be together again.</i>

304
00:17:55,867 --> 00:17:57,233
Dad, I'll help you.

305
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:00,200
It's hard to do this alone.

306
00:18:00,333 --> 00:18:03,233
<i>It'll be easier to find Berdugo
if you have someone with you.</i>

307
00:18:03,733 --> 00:18:06,400
Dad, I just don't want anything
bad to happen to you.

308
00:18:07,067 --> 00:18:08,533
Joey, don't.

309
00:18:09,433 --> 00:18:10,833
Just go home.

310
00:18:10,967 --> 00:18:12,833
Stay with your mother.

311
00:18:12,967 --> 00:18:16,000
Tell her you talked to me
and that I'm alive.

312
00:18:16,133 --> 00:18:18,833
But don't text or call me...

313
00:18:19,733 --> 00:18:21,433
so we stay safe.

314
00:18:22,033 --> 00:18:23,267
But, Dad, Andrew is with me
right now,

315
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:25,233
and we also have an agent
from the DDE.

316
00:18:25,367 --> 00:18:27,000
We can help you.

317
00:18:27,633 --> 00:18:29,900
Joey, don't insist.

318
00:18:30,633 --> 00:18:32,767
No one can know that I'm alive.

319
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:34,200
<i> It's too dangerous.</i>

320
00:18:34,333 --> 00:18:36,100
Trust is hard...

321
00:18:37,067 --> 00:18:38,933
Even with Andrew?

322
00:18:42,367 --> 00:18:43,400
Okay, fine.

323
00:18:43,533 --> 00:18:45,733
Just make sure you handle
everything in Valmora.

324
00:18:45,867 --> 00:18:48,033
We're counting on you.

325
00:18:54,733 --> 00:18:56,467
Boss, everything's set.

326
00:18:56,633 --> 00:18:58,567
We already have
a local contact there

327
00:18:58,700 --> 00:19:02,367
to make sure your transaction
with Delilah goes smoothly.

328
00:19:03,167 --> 00:19:04,767
Good.

329
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:07,233
Let's keep these people
on our payroll.

330
00:19:08,067 --> 00:19:11,900
They'll also be our men
once we take over Valmora.

331
00:19:12,033 --> 00:19:13,667
We're close, Boss.

332
00:19:14,233 --> 00:19:16,867
After that, our expansion
continues.

333
00:19:18,767 --> 00:19:20,867
Valmora now...

334
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,967
Soon, the entire Philippines.

335
00:19:25,667 --> 00:19:28,167
Dear, no one must know
that I'm alive.

336
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:30,833
Don't call this number.

337
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,667
Wait for my call.

338
00:19:35,633 --> 00:19:37,533
Yes, Dad, please be careful.

339
00:19:38,933 --> 00:19:40,400
I love you, Dad.

340
00:19:44,733 --> 00:19:46,267
<i> Joey.</i>

341
00:19:51,667 --> 00:19:53,667
Who were you talking to?

342
00:20:05,833 --> 00:20:07,533
My mom.

343
00:20:22,833 --> 00:20:25,200
There's this woman
on my radar, Delilah.

344
00:20:25,333 --> 00:20:27,200
Looks like Berdugo is meeting
someone here.

345
00:20:27,333 --> 00:20:28,067
It might be her.

346
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:29,400
Andrew, just stay put.

347
00:20:29,533 --> 00:20:32,167
My plan is to get close to her,
I'll handle it.

348
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:33,800
So what now?
Are we at a dead end?

349
00:20:33,933 --> 00:20:34,767
I've got an idea.

350
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:36,100
Since we're already here, right?

351
00:20:36,267 --> 00:20:38,633
I called earlier for a suite.

352
00:20:38,767 --> 00:20:40,667
I didn't expect
to have neighbors.

353
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:42,133
Let's just follow
Joey and Andrew.

354
00:20:42,267 --> 00:20:43,133
We can help them too.

355
00:20:43,267 --> 00:20:44,167
If this is what I need to do

356
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:46,200
to help my father,
I'll do it.

357
00:20:46,333 --> 00:20:47,400
What are you doing there?

358
00:20:47,533 --> 00:20:49,400
Just make sure
he doesn't ruin my plan.

359
00:20:49,533 --> 00:20:51,400
Francis, the owner
of this resort.

360
00:20:52,467 --> 00:20:53,533
Everything is ready

361
00:20:53,667 --> 00:20:55,333
for your guests' arrival,
Madam Delilah.

362
00:20:55,467 --> 00:20:56,867
If this deal goes South...

363
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:59,233
I stand to lose a lot.
